{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GVSPJjV64QeyKWpGzye1it","type":"tool_result","content":"    evidence: >\n      Found by the reviewers of e39s03 in attack mode on 2026-10-10. The owner bounded the attack to what a branch\n      exposes (`D-89`, précision du 2026-10-10) and left this to confining the sessions.\n    risk_level: medium\n    follow_ups: >\n      Confine the cycle's sessions so that they cannot write `~/.495/cycle/` nor `.git/config`, or replace them by 495's\n      confined Pi worker.\n    status: open\n  - bug_id: BUG-2026-10-10T151609\n    date: \"2026-10-10\"\n    title: \"The cycle writes into the registry the severity the arbitration retains without checking that it is low, medium or high, nor that a reason comes with it\"\n    severity: low\n    priority: p3\n    scope: cycle\n    what_happened: >\n      `arbitrer` (`cycle/src/automate.ts`) reads the `gravites` of the arbitration's output and `retenirGravites` writes\n      each `gravite` into `specs/bugs/registry.yaml` and the journal as it comes. Only the schema passed to\n      `claude --json-schema` limits it to `low`, `medium` or `high` and requires `raison`; the tool checks neither, and\n      the fake claude of the tests ignores the schema, so every mutant of that schema survives.\n    what_expected: >\n      A retained severity outside `low`, `medium` and `high`, or one without its reason, stops the story naming the\n      defect, as a defect with no retained severity does.\n    steps_to_reproduce:\n      - \"Give the arbitration of a story whose branch records one defect a fake claude that returns `gravites: [{ bug_id, gravite: \\\"critical\\\", raison: \\\"\\\" }]`.\"\n      - \"The agreement is recorded and the registry carries `severity: critical`, which `defautsOuverts` orders as low.\"\n    root_cause: >\n      The output of the arbitration is cast to its type and trusted; the schema is the only check of its fields.\n    evidence: >\n      Introduced by the branch of the story e39s04. Found by mutation in the first review round (the mutants of the\n      schema of `gravites` survive).\n    risk_level: low\n    follow_ups: >\n      Refuse, in `arbitrer`, a retained severity outside the three the registry reads or without a reason, with a test\n      in `arbitrage-gravite.test.ts` where the arbitration returns one.\n    status: open\n  - bug_id: BUG-2026-10-10T163128\n    date: \"2026-10-10\"\n    title: \"No test holds the path where the arbitration adds a severity to a defect of the branch that carries none\"\n    severity: low\n    priority: p3\n    scope: cycle\n    what_happened: >\n      When an entry the branch records has no `severity`, `fixerGravite` (`cycle/src/registre.ts`) adds the retained\n      one through `ajouterApres`, after the last pair of the entry. A throwaway probe shows it writes the severity, in a\n      block entry as in a flow entry, but no test of the cycle runs that path: the mutants of `ajouterApres` (line 125\n      made always true) and of its call in `fixerGravite` (line 198) survive.\n    what_expected: >\n      A test of `arbitrage-gravite.test.ts` where the branch records an entry with no severity, in block and in flow\n      form, and the registry carries the retained severity once afterwards.\n    steps_to_reproduce:\n      - \"Mutate `cycle/src/registre.ts:198` to pass `noeud.items` or line 125 to `true`; run `node --test test/cycle/arbitrage-gravite.test.ts test/cycle/registre.test.ts`: every test stays green.\"\n    root_cause: >\n      Every entry the tests add carries a severity, as the story's Given sets one.\n    evidence: >\n      Introduced by the branch of the story e39s04. Found by mutation in the first review round.\n    risk_level: low\n    follow_ups: >\n      Add the test; it adds no behaviour.\n    status: open\n  - bug_id: BUG-2026-10-10T163129\n    date: \"2026-10-10\"\n    title: \"No test holds the read-back that refuses a registry edit which would read otherwise than intended\"\n    severity: low\n    priority: p3\n    scope: cycle\n    what_happened: >\n      `verifier` (`cycle/src/registre.ts`) reads back the text `fixerGravite` and `marquerCorrige` are about to write\n      and refuses it when a YAML reader reads other items than intended. Emptying its body, or making its condition\n      false, leaves `arbitrage-gravite`, `registre` and `suite` green: on every form the tests write, the edit reads back\n      as intended, so the guard is never reached.\n    what_expected: >\n      A test where an edit of the source tokens would read back otherwise, and the registry is left as it was with\n      the story stopped naming the registry.\n    steps_to_reproduce:\n      - \"Replace `if (!isDeepStrictEqual(lus, attendus))` with `if (false)` in `cycle/src/registre.ts`; run the cycle's registry and arbitration tests: they stay green.\"\n    root_cause: >\n      The guard is defensive; no registry form the tests use makes a token edit read back differently.\n    evidence: >\n      Introduced by the branch of the story e39s04. Found by mutation by both reviewers of the first round.\n    risk_level: low\n    follow_ups: >\n      Find a registry form where a token edit reads back differently and hold the refusal with it, or drop the guard if\n      no such form exists.\n    status: open\n  - bug_id: BUG-2026-10-10T163130\n    date: \"2026-10-10\"\n    title: \"No test holds the refusal of an item that is not a defect when the branch adds it first in the bugs list\"\n    severity: low\n    priority: p3\n    scope: cycle\n    what_happened: >\n      `defautsInscrits` (`cycle/src/registre.ts`) stops the story when the branch adds to `bugs` an item that is not a\n      defect with a `bug_id`, through `etranger >= 0`. The tests always place that item after the entry of the base, so\n      the mutant `etranger > 0` survives: with it, such an item in first position would pass without stopping the story.\n    what_expected: >\n      A test where the item that is not a defect is the first of the list, and the story stops naming entry 1.\n    steps_to_reproduce:\n      - \"Replace `etranger >= 0` with `etranger > 0` in `cycle/src/registre.ts`; run `node --test test/cycle/arbitrage-gravite.test.ts`: every test stays green.\"\n    root_cause: >\n      The test of the foreign item puts it after the base entry, never at index 0.\n    evidence: >\n      Introduced by the branch of the story e39s04. Found by mutation by both reviewers of the first round.\n    risk_level: low\n    follow_ups: >\n      Add the test; it adds no behaviour.\n    status: open\n  - bug_id: BUG-2026-10-10T163131\n    date: \"2026-10-10\"\n    title: \"A defect written under a root key of the registry other than bugs is neither weighed by the arbitration nor refused\"\n    severity: low\n    priority: p3\n    scope: cycle\n    what_happened: >\n      `lire` (`cycle/src/registre.ts`) reads only the `bugs` key of the registry's root and ignores every other key. A\n      branch that writes a defect under another key (`other:` with a `- bug_id:` item) records it in the registry's\n      file with the severity its session chose; the arbitration does not weigh it, the tool does not stop, and the\n      agreement is recorded (throwaway probe of the second reviewer).\n    what_expected: >\n      A key of the registry's root other than `bugs` stops the story naming the registry, as an item of `bugs` that\n      is not a defect does.\n    steps_to_reproduce:\n      - \"On a story branch, append `other:\\\\n  - bug_id: BUG-2026-10-10T000001\\\\n    severity: low\\\\n    status: open\\\\n` to `specs/bugs/registry.yaml` and commit.\"\n      - \"Run the arbitration: `defautsInscrits` returns no defect for it, `continuer` is true and the agreement is recorded.\"\n    root_cause: >\n      The reader looks up `bugs` among the root's pairs and refuses nothing else on the root but a non-map.\n    evidence: >\n      Introduced by the branch of the story e39s04, which replaced the line-by-line reading by a YAML reader. Found by\n      the second reviewer of the first round. A YAML reader does not count the item in `bugs` either, so it was not\n      classed as a bypass.\n    risk_level: low\n    follow_ups: >\n      Refuse, in `lire`, a root key other than `bugs`, with a test in `arbitrage-gravite.test.ts`; it adds a refusal.\n    status: open\n  - bug_id: BUG-2026-10-10T163920\n    date: \"2026-10-10\"\n    title: \"No test tells the landing of the last story of an epic in auto from the same landing without auto\"\n    severity: low\n    priority: p3\n    scope: cycle\n    what_happened: >\n      `marquerVersee` (`cycle/src/main.ts`) runs the phase of medium repairs only when the story landed under\n      `cycle <story> auto` and is the last of its epic, through `!auto || !derniereDeSonEpic(...)`. The test of the end\n      of an epic (`test/cycle/auto-fin-d-epic.test.ts`) always lands in `auto`, so dropping `!auto ||` leaves it green:\n      with that mutant, a last story landed without `auto` would start the repairs.\n    what_expected: >\n      A test where the last story of an epic lands without `auto`, and no session of repairs runs.\n    steps_to_reproduce:\n      - \"Replace `if (!auto || !derniereDeSonEpic(lirePlan(ctx.root), id))` with `if (!derniereDeSonEpic(lirePlan(ctx.root), id))` in `cycle/src/main.ts`; run `node --test test/cycle/auto-fin-d-epic.test.ts`: it stays green.\"\n    root_cause: >\n      The test exercises the last story and another story, both in `auto`, never a landing without it.\n    evidence: >\n      Found by mutation by a reviewer of the last round of the story e39s04, on a line outside its diff.\n    risk_level: low\n    follow_ups: >\n      Add the test; it adds no behaviour.\n    status: open","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3ab0465-5d2b-4167-b5ba-802066126ed8","uuid":"60908e43-6167-45db-b0f6-0bd196201669","timestamp":"2026-10-10T14:56: